Literal expander and normalizer: what the port lowers, measured 2026-11-12.
Occurrences are the port's parser counts over src/compiler/**/*.iyi and src/iyi/*.iyi,
as printed by the transform gate's corpus section.

Ported in src/compiler/semantic/literal_expander.iyi (fixtures and mutations in the gate):
  ArrayLiteral          1795   expand_array, expand_named_array, expand_hash (HashLiteral 17)
  Case                   310   subject, tuple subject (tuple_when_comparison), when chains
  MultiAssign             54   values, single value, splat, call targets, strict count
  Select                  --   select lowering, binds_it off for its own case
  RangeLiteral            31
  StringInterpolation   1363   contiguous literal merge
  And                   1902   expand_and (left side tested in place, else bound to a temporary)
  Or                    1656   expand_or (same forms as And)
  Def                     --   walks receiver, argument defaults, body (shared transformer does not)
  Arg                     --   walks default value and restriction

Walked but left as written (the hosted walk does not enter them either):
  MacroIf 183, MacroFor 20, MacroExpression 11, Macro 3

Not ported (occurrences in the port's own source):
  RegexLiteral            3   hosted expand(RegexLiteral) with Regex.new and options
  ProcLiteral             2   hosted expand(ProcLiteral)
  ProcPointer             0   listed for completeness
  Propagate               1   expand not yet read
  Defer                   4   expand not yet read
  NamedTupleLiteral       1   hosted has no expansion either (comment in literal_expander.iyi)
  Unless                940   normalizer side: status not yet measured here
  Until                   7   normalizer side: status not yet measured here
  OpAssign              187   normalizer side: status not yet measured here

Not hidden by the shared Node token any more (the corpus gate lists each one with its count):
  ImportDecl 482, UsingDecl 431, ModuleHeader 114, PointerOf 118, MagicConstant 18,
  Require 15, SizeOf 1, ReadInstanceVar 1. Their children are not compared.

Corpus (transform gate section 6): 131 of 135 files identical, 1 refused by the port
(native/wasm/leb.iyi:8:10, a parser panic), 3 differing:
  bind.iyi    case left as Case where the hosted walk produced If (first diff at line 54)
  ast.iyi     Call "==" over Call "&" differs (first diff at line 115)
  token.iyi   cmp differs but diff prints no hunk: investigate the bytes first
